Subject: [PATCH] enable retained Gralloc3/2 fallback for the M4 Hybrid Vendor

# Reason: the V6 runtime trial reaches SurfaceFlinger but aborts gralloc-mapper is missing. BZI6 libui's API-level>35 branch skips its retained genuine Gralloc3/2 implementations after mapper5/4 fail on star2lte.
# Affected: M4 runtime helper/lock, restore metadata loop and real-ext4 gate. Change one four-byte conditional branch to NOP only in the exact locked BZI6 libui. Keep mapper5/4 preference, mapper2/3 isLoaded tests, allocator checks, OS properties and every other library byte.
# Verify: full input/output hash and executable-segment/context/branch-target checks; exact four-byte diff and reverse; idempotence/replacement and wrong-M2/N scope negatives; actual ext4 byte/owner/mode/label fixture; complete source replay. Runtime result remains separate.
# Rollback: reverse0193 and its series/lock entry; diagnostic SYSTEM libui must restore the original locked bytes/metadata. No kernel/vendor/radio/EFS or version-property change.

